#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166633 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "2281e86d-4f21-53da-b6fa-1f178d4862a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8433" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int} \\dfrac{1}{1+\\sinh^2 x} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x + \\sin^2 x= 1\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2x -\\sinh^2x=1\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n1+\\sinh^2x=\\cosh^2x\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\sech x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{1}{1 + \\sinh^{2} x}dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{\\cosh^{2} x}dx \\\\\n&= \\int(\\frac{1}{\\cosh x})^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\intsech^{2} xdx \\\\\n&= \\tanh x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166634 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97c01757-f2bf-5b7b-b51b-ff490b54f555" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "9b63d35a-f1c5-554f-ac4c-68d18afa153a" :question/math-academy-id "e-8434" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2} \\dfrac{\\tanh{x}-\\tanh^3{x}}{\\sech{x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1 + \\tan^2 x= \\sec^2{x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-\\tanh^2x=\\sech^2{x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\ln 2}\\frac{\\tanh x - \\tanh^{3} x}{sech x}dx &= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2}((1 - \\tanh^{2} x)\\tanh x)/(sech x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2}\\frac{sech^{2} x\\tanh x}{sech x}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2}sech x\\tanh xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.- sech x\\right|_{0}^{\\ln 2} \\\\\n&=-sech (\\ln 2) + sech 0 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{e^{\\ln 2} + e^{-\\ln 2}} + \\frac{2}{e^{0} + e^{0}} \\\\\n&= - (2)/((2 + \\frac{1}{2})) + 1 \\\\\n&= - (2)/((\\frac{5}{2})) + 1 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{4}{5} + 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166635 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f377f3-700a-57a9-96e5-954aed678e62" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "7af9f5f6-1e14-55ea-8a09-25d211cb40d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-8435" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\ln 5} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\coth^2x - 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n1 + \\cot^2 x= \\csc^2{x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osbourn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n\\coth^2x - 1=\\csch^2{x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int_{0}^{\\ln 5} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\coth^2x - 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x &= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 5} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\csch^2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 5} \\dfrac{1}{\\csch{x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &= \\int_{0}^{\\ln 5} \\sinh{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &= \\left.\\cosh{x} \\, \\Big\\right|_{0}^{\\ln 5} \\\\[5pt] &= \\cosh(\\ln{5}) - \\cosh{0} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac{e^{\\ln{5}}+e^{-\\ln{5}}}{2} - \\dfrac{e^0+e^0}{2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac{\\left(5+\\dfrac 1 5\\right)}{2} - \\dfrac{1+1}{2} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac{13}{5} - 1 \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac{8}{5} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166636 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a95e37c6-66f4-5a70-87e8-31f3694a20a4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/id #uuid "14733493-2ad9-5fc2-9afe-26384f6ce9ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-8436" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{2}{\\cosh^2(2x+1)-1} \\, \\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 \\theta - \\sinh^2 \\theta = 1\n$$\n\nSetting\n\n$$\n\\theta = 2x + 1\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 (2x+1) - \\sinh^2(2x+1) = 1\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 (2x+1) -1 = \\sinh^2(2x+1)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(2)/(\\cosh^{2} (2x + 1) - 1)dx &= 2\\int(1)/(\\sinh^{2} (2x + 1))dx \\\\\n&= 2\\intcsch^{2} (2x + 1)dx \\\\\n&=-\\coth (2x + 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86011b4a-1991-599e-87dc-bd7a622ca938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-sech x - \\sinh x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165657} {:answer/id #uuid "91c96317-2f89-5a69-9d6d-0f6e56f27598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\coth x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165658} {:answer/id #uuid "a284de24-9130-5567-84d2-0489d2b489a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "sech x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165659} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb58fad-2eef-54ed-86ac-5789c66d56dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\coth x + \\cosh x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165660} {:answer/id #uuid "efb20805-8df8-59db-977a-8ae57e19e376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\coth x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165661}] :answer-field/id #uuid "526dd014-553b-5336-80a3-305b2a62ee6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165656}] :question/id #uuid "73150534-b7bb-5cf7-bc82-812c547a0e7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-95837" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\coth^{2} x}{\\sinh^{2} x + 1}dx$."}]}
